{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unhygienic-houndlike-arrowworm","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe configuration layer carries machinery for a compatibility story this breaking release ends: a legacy env-alias map (`_config_sources.py:333-339`) and a config-key alias table (`_config_sections.py:198`, consumed at `:243-250`, re-exported through `_config_schema.py:32`, `config.py:9,45,56,384-385`, `show_config.py:142-146`); 13 warn-class tombstones in `_deprecations.py` beside 6 error rows; two test hooks read from production env vars (`REBAR_HLC_NOW` in `hlc.py:57-67`, `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` in `compact_txn.py:179-195`); two copies of the precedence resolver inside `config.py` (`_resolve:442-466` vs `resolve_with_sources:774-800`) plus three copies of user-then-project file discovery, with `config.py` sitting at exactly the 800-line cap; an env registry that hand-lists 40 of 104 canonical names; and 54 importers of the `_engine_support/resolver.py` re-export shim plus the `reducer/_processors.py:18-31` re-exports (ADR 0111 forbids internal shims). Unknown `[llm]` keys are silently ignored even under `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error` because `[llm]` is a reserved section (`_config_sections.py:187,201`). The operator ruled (2026-09-06): hard cutover, no aliases, warn tombstones removed, error rows kept with real `removed_in` versions, unknown-key warnings kept as the forward-compatibility mechanism and extended to `[llm]`. Every claim is verified on origin/main 083620b0 in this epic's first comment.\n\nOperator sanction recorded here: the alias-deletion and test-hook stories remove censused `env_var` mechanisms, so each runs `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change (`tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364`; precedent commit 81da792) and says so in its commit message.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No importer of `rebar._engine_support.resolver` or of the `reducer/_processors.py` re-exports remains; both shims are deleted. Checked by the repo-wide grep and `make verify` in the shim story.\n- [ ] No env or config alias resolves; `_deprecations.py` holds exactly the 6 error rows with real `removed_in` versions; an unknown `[llm]` key warns under the same policy as other sections. Checked by the alias story's tests and the config-surface golden.\n- [ ] `REBAR_HLC_NOW` and `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` are not read by production code; tests inject the clock and the rename barrier through `tests/_child_hooks.py`. Checked by the hook story's grep and its child-process tests.\n- [ ] `config.py` has one precedence composer and one file-discovery function, is under 800 lines, and `resolve`/`resolve_with_sources`/`show_config` produce byte-identical output to before. Checked by the composer story's goldens.\n- [ ] The env registry derives all 104 canonical names, the canary `github-api` source is retired, and CHANGELOG entries for the removed names and `REBAR_HLC=0` are correct. Checked by the registry story's generator `--check` and the CHANGELOG review.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- S1 migrate resolver and `_processors` re-export importers, delete the shims (LAND FIRST, priority 1): criterion 1.\n- S2 delete alias machinery, prune warn tombstones, warn on unknown `[llm]` keys: criterion 2; depends on S1 and on the overlap epic's `overlap_*` removal story.\n- S3 test hooks out of production: criterion 3; depends on S2.\n- S4 one precedence composer and one discovery: criterion 4; depends on S3.\n- S5 env registry derives every canonical name, retire the canary source, CHANGELOG bookkeeping: criterion 5; depends on S4.","id":"e12f-a994-29d3-4f72","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Config and env cleanup: delete aliases and warn tombstones, evict test hooks, unify precedence, remove internal shims"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788806609072694182,"uuid":"cc299a8e-9bda-4cfb-9d25-193cff31ec73"}